# Any other ?id= (a deleted guide) lands on the index rather than a dead end.
/guide.html  id=:id  /guides.html  301

# Slugs that have been renamed. One hop, never a chain: every entry points
# at the guide's current URL, not at the slug that replaced it.

# Trailing-slash normalisation for the clean URLs.
/guides/:slug  /guides/:slug/  301!
/topics/:slug  /topics/:slug/  301!
/ages/:slug    /ages/:slug/    301!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unknown guide slugs — must stay last.
#
# This build wrote a real file for every guide above, and Netlify serves a
# real file in preference to any non-forced rule. So anything still
# reaching this line is a guide that does not exist, and it gets a genuine
# 404 — not a styled 'not found' page returning 200, which would leave
# Google indexing dead URLs as though they were real ones.
#
# The committed fallback _redirects in the repository does the opposite:
# it rewrites to guide.html with a 200 so that every guide still renders
# if this build never ran. That file only survives when this one is not
# generated, so the two can never both apply.
/guides/*  /404.html  404
